      "content": "The issue lies in the `paginate` function. The problem is that it starts slicing the list from `page * page_size`, which means the first page starts from index `0` when `page` is `1`. However, it should start from index `0` when `page` is `1`, and so on.\n\nLet's modify the `start` calculation to subtract `page_size` when `page` is `1`. This will ensure that the first page starts from index `0`.\n\nHere is the corrected `paginate` function:\n\n```python\ndef paginate(items, page, page_size):\n    \"\"\"Return the items shown on `page`. Pages are numbered from 1.\"\"\"\n    start = (page - 1) * page_size\n    end = start + page_size\n    return items[start:end]\n```\n\nNow, I'll apply this change to the file.\n",
